{"kind":"request","text":"S2: artroom-scope runs the scope index in enforce mode\n\nPlanner work, from the attack-surface review of 10 November 2026\n(planner request 79daff0f, finding 1.5). The live Worker and its tracked\nfile select `register`. In that mode an unknown, well-formed scope ID\nmakes a new object with the full schema, and no window bounds it. The\nother four Workers run `enforce`.\n\nSteps:\n1. List every room of artroom-scope and each of its scopes. The cutover\n   needs the same inventory.\n2. Reach each listed scope while the Worker still runs `register`, and\n   read the index to confirm each row.\n3. One head: `SCOPE_INDEX_MODE` is \"enforce\" in\n   apps/room/wrangler.artroom-scope.jsonc, and the comment above it says\n   what is true. Checker review. Ruling 5b38cde5 holds: the deploy\n   command takes no override.\n4. Land the head between two builder landings, deploy artroom-scope with\n   START and END acts, and check that a listed scope answers and that an\n   unknown ID answers the enforce refusal.\n\nA room that the inventory missed is refused after step 4. The data\nstays. A deploy of the previous version restores it, and I then add the\nroom to the list.\n\nDone when the live setting reads \"enforce\" and the check of step 4 is\nrecorded.","body":{"conditions":"The live SCOPE_INDEX_MODE of artroom-scope reads enforce, the tracked file agrees through a reviewed head, and the check of a listed scope and an unknown ID is recorded.","target_head":"7177b87be03ced9e2ddae2a5ebfcdfffcc1fda62","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}